      "name": "service_quality_theme",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.95,
      "source_groundedness": 0.9,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "A well-differentiated categorical axis (warm/cold/inconsistent/absent) directly serving the exploratory query on airline service. Samples map soundly to source text; the 'cold_impersonal' tag on a seat-focused complaint is a slight stretch but defensible."
    },
    {
      "name": "service_decline_signal",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.55,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "A boolean flag adds some analytical leverage for trend/decline framing, but it is a bare true/false with modest new information beyond the theme column. Sample values (all false) are consistent with positive/neutral texts."
    },
    {
      "name": "cost_cutting_perception",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.6,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Distinct latent concept (perceived cost-cutting) that offers a real analytical angle, though as a rare boolean its leverage is limited. Sample values grounded and correctly false where text gives no cost-cutting cues."
    },
    {
      "name": "food_quality_theme",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.9,
      "source_groundedness": 0.92,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Rich multi-valued categorization (excellent/acceptable/poor/special_meal_failure/ran_out) giving a strong grouping axis. NULLs for silent rows are appropriate. Samples map well; 'acceptable' for a food-silent review is a mild over-assertion but minor."
    },
    {
      "name": "seat_comfort_issue_type",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.92,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Useful typology of seat problems giving a fresh axis beyond the numeric Seat Comfort rating. Well grounded in samples (narrow_poor_padding, excellent_spacious) with correct NULLs for silent rows."
    },
    {
      "name": "cabin_hardware_condition",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.7,
      "source_groundedness": 0.75,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Reasonable new axis on aircraft condition. However 'standard_adequate' dominates (571) and is applied to rows with no hardware mention (e.g. sample 5), suggesting a default-fill that asserts a condition the text does not support, weakening groundedness somewhat."
    },
    {
      "name": "disruption_handling_quality",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.75,
      "source_groundedness": 0.95,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Captures how disruptions were handled, a genuinely distinct axis; 'not_applicable' correctly dominates for the many disruption-free reviews and samples are consistent."
    },
    {
      "name": "ground_service_issue",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.8,
      "source_groundedness": 0.95,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Adds a ground-experience dimension absent from original columns (check-in, booking, lounge, baggage). Well grounded; 'none_mentioned' appropriately used for silent samples."
    },
    {
      "name": "premium_class_value_perception",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.7,
      "source_groundedness": 0.7,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "A value-perception scale is useful, but overlaps conceptually with the existing 'Value For Money' rating, and the four-way split is applied even to rows with little value discussion, producing inferred values (e.g. 'meets_expectation') that the text only weakly supports."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.82,
  "source_groundedness": 0.87,
  "rationale": "The added columns provide a diverse, well-differentiated set of aspect-level axes (service, food, seat, cabin, disruption, ground, value) that genuinely help the open-ended exploratory query about which aspect is worth analyzing. Most are multi-valued with meaningful distributions and correct use of NULL/not_applicable for silent rows. Weaknesses: two boolean flags add limited leverage, premium_class_value_perception partly duplicates the existing Value For Money rating, and cabin_hardware_condition/value columns appear to default-fill non-null categories onto rows that are silent, a mild groundedness concern. No outright fabrications observed in the samples."
}

